e peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $5.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $373K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["LTC Properties, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $2.5B market cap on $263M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $129M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.0% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 42% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4204712812960236},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 55% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (83% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Q4 Earnings Estimate for LTC Properties Issued By Huntington","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/q4-earnings-estimate-for-ltc-properties-issued-by-huntington.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793969031.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"LTC Properties (NYSE:LTC) Announces Earnings Resu