above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 7 covering analysts target $45.86 on average, 2% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 5% falls short of the cost of capital of 6.6%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.34).","It converts 49% of revenue into free cash flow, or 45% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.15x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 49%.","ROE of 11% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 23pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.4x net debt to EBITDA ($14.4M of cash against $842.2M of debt), with interest covered 6.2x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 14.5% over 3 years, 10.5% over 5 years and 6.8% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.3% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+1.9% trend).","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 3.2% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.2x depreciation (2.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.0%, and institutions hold 81%.","Insider trading is two-way: 5 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $643K bought.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.3% (5.1% in dividends, less 4.0% of net share issuance).","The share count has grown 6.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 24 consecutive years, raising it 3.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 25 employees, each generates about $10.5M of revenue, 4.6x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 8.4% a year.","That works out to $5.1M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $373K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":65,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread) and it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 45, gates 12/26)","Trades 47% below fair value of $83.71","FCF margin 49.0%","Revenue grew 10.5%/yr over 5y","P/E 4.5x vs sector 23.6x"],"cons":["ROIC 5.5% vs WACC 6.6%","Net debt/EBITDA 3.4x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","EV/EBITDA 23.1x vs sector 16.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":71.15,"vc":{"base":83.71,"base_src":"dcf","bear":49.32,"bull":140.98,"alt_median":54.5,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.5779,"dispersion":0.3121,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (31% dispersion)","DCF is 158% above the other models' median ($54.50)"]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"LTC","date":"2026-11-06"}